A console-based User Management System developed in C that allows users to register and log in using stored credentials.
User information is saved using file handling, making the data persistent across program executions.

Features-
* User Registration
* User Login
* Duplicate username detection
* Password masking support (optional future enhancement)
* Input validation
* Persistent storage using files
* Colorful terminal interface

Concepts Used-
* Structures
* Functions
* File Handling
* String Handling
* Input Validation
* Menu-Driven Programming

Project Structure-

Each user record stores:
* Username
* Password

Data is stored in a file and can be accessed even after restarting the application.

Sample Menu-
1. Register
2. Login
3. Exit

Learning Outcomes-
  This project helped me practice:
  * User authentication logic
  * File-based data storage
  * Working with strings
  * Preventing duplicate records
  * Creating reusable functions
  * Building interactive CLI applications


